From 4de0ac66b1fa9550381774d4aacb39971cf53663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:16:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: what the second reading of the display watch
 found

The question of the display watch took no answer at all. It told that the
dialog still showed its own question by the heading of the dialog, after the
dialog had closed; and a dialog box forgets its heading, its text and its
buttons as it closes (CGUIDialogBoxBase::OnDeinitWindow()). Every answer
was taken for one to another question: the user was asked three times and
Kodi never moved, nor did it remember that the user had said to stay.

The dialog box now keeps what it showed when it was last closed and counts
its closes (GetClosed(), in place of GetHeading()). An answer is taken when
the dialog was closed once since the question was put and showed that
question, heading and text, when it was.

Also:

- A dialog that is left open behind the loop that waits for it is closed.
  That loop ends when Kodi stops drawing (its display was put to sleep),
  with the dialog still there: it came back as a question whose buttons
  did nothing, and kept the watch from asking.
- While Kodi does not draw, nobody can be asked. It is as with a question
  that nobody answers, at once: Kodi moves when nothing plays and it has
  not moved unasked often enough; else the question waits for the display
  to be awake.
- An offer of which nothing comes is made again after a new look at the
  outputs, which are taken as they were before it: the display has to be
  there still, and so has it where Kodi shows itself on no output and waits
  for what plays to end. Before, three tries in a row ended it for good,
  and on no output Kodi was started again for a display that could have
  gone. The wait grows from 30 seconds to two minutes; a question that was
  shown and came to nothing is shown three times at most.
- The question says what no answer does: where Kodi would not move by
  itself (something plays, or it has been started again unasked twice) it
  does not say that it will.
- Kodi on no output: what the start that looked for an output saw is what a
  later look is compared with (the outputs of a single device are kept also
  when none can be used), and where that is not known the first look is
  taken at once. It was taken ten seconds or more after the start, so that
  a TV that answered within them was never new.
- The end of Dolby Vision output tells the watch from where the output is
  put back (EndDVBridge()), which is also where it is tried again every
  second after a display refused it.
- Kodi stopping with the question open is not taken for "stay". Looks that
  fail are tried again after longer each time, and given up after six
  unless nothing is known yet.

The host test: the check that what happens to the output in use is no
reason to move used an output that could not rank above itself. It uses a
TV that comes back as one that takes Dolby Vision, and shows that under the
name it was given at the start it would be offered.

The question, the dialog box and the thread are in code that the host
test does not reach: read and compiled, not run on a graphics device.
